.TH "GF-ACCESS-CONTROL-REMOVE-USER-ROLE" "1" "Jun 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-access-control-remove-user-role - Removes a user role assignment


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf access-control remove-user-role [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a user role assignment

.PP
Revoke a role from a user. For bulk updates consider Set user role assignments.

.PP
You need to have a permission with action \fBusers.roles:remove\fR and scope \fBpermissions:type:delegate\fR\&. \fBpermissions:type:delegate\fR scope ensures that users can only unassign roles which have same, or a subset of permissions which the user has. For example, if a user does not have required permissions for creating users, they won’t be able to unassign a role which will allow to do that. This is done to prevent escalation of privileges.

.PP
Response schema (RemoveUserRoleOK.Payload):
  message  string


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--describe-response-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the response payload and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB--global\fP[=false]
	A flag indicating if the assignment is global or not. If set to false, the default org ID of the authenticated user will be used from the request to remove assignment.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove-user-role

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	Print the raw HTTP response body instead of the decoded payload

.PP
\fB--role-uid\fP=""
	RoleUID [required]

.PP
\fB--user-id\fP=0
	UserID [required]


